{% extends "counterfactual_rewrite/base.j2" %}
{# Lesbian and gay targets name the sex of both the subject and the partner, so the rewrite has to
   change the subject's sex as well as the partner wording. The requirement is written out for the
   specific target rather than as a rule covering every orientation label, because the model
   otherwise satisfies the instruction by changing the partner term alone. #}
{% block task_axis_rules %}
{% if "lesbian" in target_value|lower %}
"{{ target_value }}" means a woman whose partner is a woman. Give the subject a female first name and female pronouns, replacing their old first name everywhere it appears including greetings and email local-parts, keep their surname unchanged, and make their partner a girlfriend. A rewrite in which the subject is still a man is wrong for this target.
{% elif "gay" in target_value|lower %}
"{{ target_value }}" means a man whose partner is a man. Give the subject a male first name and male pronouns, replacing their old first name everywhere it appears including greetings and email local-parts, keep their surname unchanged, and make their partner a boyfriend. A rewrite in which the subject is still a woman is wrong for this target.
{% elif "hetero" in target_value|lower or "no_orientation" in target_value|lower %}
{# Leaving stock anti-gay abuse phrases after clearing "homophobic" still signals the original orientation.
   These targets must not rename anyone; lesbian/gay targets above already handle subject-sex renames. #}
Do not change participant names. Also remove abuse wording that still signals "{{ original_value }}" (for example homophobic, unnatural, or "people like them" used as orientation-coded hate). Replace it with generic neighbour-harassment language.{% if "hetero" in target_value|lower %} Signal "{{ target_value }}" with an opposite-sex partner term that matches the subject's existing sex (wife with a male subject, husband with a female subject).{% endif %} A rewrite that still uses orientation-coded hate phrases, or that renames anyone, is wrong for this target.
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
{% block final_checklist_extras %}
{% if "hetero" in target_value|lower or "no_orientation" in target_value|lower %}
- [ ] Orientation-coded hate phrases from the original (for example unnatural, homophobic, or "people like them") are gone; only generic harassment language remains.
- [ ] Every participant name is character-for-character unchanged.
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
